{"kind":"request","text":"codex: close a review-filing papercut at the write boundary, so the merge-driven succession gate can never be surprised at merge time. Today (2026-08-13) an approved design review could not be merged because the approval report rested only on its promise, not on the artifact it names; gs merge refused at cmd/gs/main.go:733 (\"approval does not rest on its named artifact\"). The unblock is a manual re-file (request 748c6edf), but the class should not recur.\n\nRoot cause, established: gs review already does the right thing — cmd/gs/main.go:56 rests the verdict on [promise, request, artifact]. The failing approval was filed via the raw state path (gs state / the MCP state tool) as kind=report with body.verdict=approved and body.artifact set, but rests_on=[promise] only. So the tool is correct; the unguarded raw path around it is the hole, and the mistake is invisible until merge.\n\nRequested fix, matching the existing write-boundary guards (the cited-retirement guard and the report-has-no-promise guard already refuse at submit): when a submitted state act is an approval report — an effective report-lifecycle kind carrying body.verdict == \"approved\" with a non-empty body.artifact — the application submit path refuses to sign unless rests_on contains that artifact event, with a message that tells the caller to add the artifact basis (or file via gs review). This turns a merge-time refusal into an immediate, legible write-time error from every surface, and it cannot make a currently-valid approval invalid because gs review already includes the artifact. Add a test that the raw path refuses an approved report naming an artifact it does not rest on, and that gs review still succeeds unchanged.\n\nAlso update the review discipline so the convention and the guard agree: AGENTS.md step 4 and SKILL.md should say a verdict is filed with gs review, or if filed by hand must rest on the artifact it names. Keep that doc change in the same head and publish/supersede its artifacts per the merge discipline.\n\nScope note: if an open request already covers a write-boundary guard for review reports, take only the doc half here and rest it on that one; do not duplicate.","body":{"conditions":"The application submit path refuses to sign an approval report (effective report-lifecycle kind, body.verdict==approved, non-empty body.artifact) whose rests_on does not contain the named artifact, with a legible message, proven by a test; gs review continues to succeed unchanged, proven by a test. AGENTS.md step 4 and SKILL.md state that a verdict is filed via gs review or must rest on the artifact it names, updated and re-anchored in the same head. No currently-valid approval is made invalid. If a write-boundary guard for review reports is already in flight, this delivers only the doc half resting on that request.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}